  "notes": [
   "Parts are unchanged from step 1.",
   "The catalogue card for arduino-mkr1000 lists only USB, VIN, VCC, GND and BAT. It has no digital pin 2. The image and schematic wire the circuit to pin 2, so wire1 connects to port '2', named as in the tutorial's pin labels. This port is not on the catalogue card.",
   "Circuit: pin 2 -> green wire -> breadboard column 3 -> 220 ohm resistor -> column 6 -> LED anode. The LED cathode is in column 8 -> black wire -> GND. The resistor is on the anode side, as in the schematic.",
   "The image shows the breadboard rows lettered j-f on the top half and a-e on the bottom half. I used the catalogue's naming instead: top half is bank 't', rows a-e. Each column strip has the same connectivity either way.",
   "The bent LED leg (column 6) is taken as the anode and the straight leg (column 8) as the cathode, as the schematic's current path requires.",
   "A1 is read in the sketch but nothing is wired to it, so it has no edge. The LED is red in the image.",
   "The 220 ohm resistor limits the LED current. The MKR 1000 logic is 3.3 V, so pin 2 drives the LED within its limits."
  ]
 },
